1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:02,712
Since the Enlightenment and the Industrial Revolution,

2
00:00:03,025 --> 00:00:04,288
we have felt like gods.

3
00:00:04,712 --> 00:00:05,562
But look at the price.

4
00:00:05,975 --> 00:00:07,075
In roughly a century,

5
00:00:07,312 --> 00:00:09,325
we have burned through fossil fuels that took

6
00:00:09,338 --> 00:00:11,700
the earth a hundred million years to store.

7
00:00:12,112 --> 00:00:13,788
Trees and ancient life,

8
00:00:14,025 --> 00:00:15,075
compressed into carbon,

9
00:00:15,438 --> 00:00:16,975
set on fire in the blink of an

10
00:00:16,988 --> 00:00:17,275
eye.

11
00:00:17,712 --> 00:00:18,862
For thousands of years,

12
00:00:19,062 --> 00:00:21,238
the human population stayed in the hundreds of

13
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:21,912
millions.

14
00:00:22,325 --> 00:00:24,162
Then it exploded into billions,

15
00:00:24,362 --> 00:00:26,500
because we found a way to borrow energy

16
00:00:26,512 --> 00:00:27,638
from the deep past.

17
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:30,888
Bach describes our situation with a striking image:

18
00:00:31,188 --> 00:00:32,925
we are skiing down the slope of an

19
00:00:32,938 --> 00:00:34,050
entropic abyss.

20
00:00:34,475 --> 00:00:35,575
We are going fast,

21
00:00:35,788 --> 00:00:36,963
it feels exhilarating,

22
00:00:37,212 --> 00:00:39,300
and almost nobody is asking how the run

23
00:00:39,312 --> 00:00:39,788
ends.

24
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,075
Look at your own life.

25
00:00:41,488 --> 00:00:43,250
You wake up in an air conditioned room,

26
00:00:43,525 --> 00:00:44,900
drive an air conditioned car,

27
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,200
and walk into an air conditioned office.

28
00:00:47,612 --> 00:00:48,900
It is a closed cooling chain.

29
00:00:49,312 --> 00:00:51,162
Our food travels the same way,

30
00:00:51,438 --> 00:00:52,738
in refrigerated trucks,

31
00:00:52,962 --> 00:00:54,275
to refrigerated shelves.

32
00:00:54,688 --> 00:00:56,450
If that chain breaks for a few days

33
00:00:56,462 --> 00:00:57,812
in a brutal heat wave,

34
00:00:58,112 --> 00:00:59,613
many people will not survive.

35
00:01:00,025 --> 00:01:01,850
We are far more fragile than we feel.

36
00:01:02,275 --> 00:01:05,275
In nature, a species that consumes its environment

37
00:01:05,287 --> 00:01:07,362
faster than it can recover behaves like a

38
00:01:07,375 --> 00:01:08,012
parasite,

39
00:01:08,425 --> 00:01:09,700
and it usually collapses.

40
00:01:10,112 --> 00:01:12,325
Our civilization is betting that we can stay

41
00:01:12,338 --> 00:01:13,675
in control of this machine.

42
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:14,938
But in Bach's view,

43
00:01:15,338 --> 00:01:17,150
it is not clear that anyone is steering.

44
00:01:17,575 --> 00:01:19,325
The machine is rolling downhill,

45
00:01:19,612 --> 00:01:21,375
and no one knows which button would stop

46
00:01:21,388 --> 00:01:21,538
it.

47
00:01:21,962 --> 00:01:23,800
So could something smarter than us pull the

48
00:01:23,812 --> 00:01:24,750
emergency brake?

49
00:01:25,162 --> 00:01:28,300
Many people hope that something is artificial intelligence.
